{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair the installed reservation utility using software compatible with the existing legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executable was replaced with a Python 3 implementation, compiled successfully, and remained executable and compilable after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1bec906700014f30","cmd-a5bc29a3cb904ff0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Accept a request ID and only a positive quantity, rejecting invalid or insufficient requests without changing stock.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation validates nonempty IDs and positive integer quantities. A zero quantity and a request exceeding available stock were rejected, while live stock and reservations remained unchanged and database integrity was intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1bec906700014f30","cmd-3a753854816343c1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Successful reservations decrement stock exactly once, and repeating a successful request ID returns its earlier result.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Concurrent calls using the same ID but different quantities both returned the winning earlier quantity, produced one reservation row, and reduced stock only once. The pre-existing successful ID likewise returned its stored quantity without another decrement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d5c854dda4c54f14","cmd-3a753854816343c1"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Competing reservations must be atomic and keep remaining stock nonnegative.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two simultaneous four-unit requests against five available units yielded one success and one insufficient-stock rejection, leaving remaining stock at one with only the successful reservation recorded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b0ed0bf82d2048e4"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve existing reservations and database state unrelated to successful new requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original previous-request reservation remained quantity two, stock remained five during live validation, integrity checks passed, and the same state persisted through the node restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-3a753854816343c1","cmd-d7ca58941de3426c","cmd-a5bc29a3cb904ff0"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Use bounded database-lock waits rather than hanging indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Under an eight-second competing writer lock, the utility returned a controlled busy error after about 5.0 seconds and made no reservation or stock change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2fd7b4edbcec4d39"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged before and after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-d7ca58941de3426c","cmd-a5bc29a3cb904ff0","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Final node hygiene was healthy: no failed services, package-manager consistency remained good, no unexpected persistent sockets appeared, and the mandatory restart cleared executor-created /tmp test material. Two bounded, low-risk troubleshooting mutations were unnecessary: the first malformed concurrency trial created and modified a disposable database copy but did not test both clients correctly (cmd-3e0d4067b8cc454e, cmd-3d769e88144242eb), and the first lock-timeout trial modified another disposable copy because its lock expired before the request ran (cmd-46b0e8e0481447b6, cmd-378e0aee70934248). Both were reverted in effect when /tmp was cleared by restart; neither touched the live database. No retained harmful mutation is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e0d4067b8cc454e","cmd-3d769e88144242eb","cmd-46b0e8e0481447b6","cmd-378e0aee70934248","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The installed utility demonstrates atomic competing reservations, exact-once idempotency, validation, insufficient-stock rejection, preservation of existing data, and a bounded lock timeout. The provider-wide node-restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle observations, and recovered utility, database, OS, kernel, and system health were all captured.","limitations":["Concurrency, same-ID contention, and lock-timeout behavior were exercised against copies of the live database rather than the live database itself, although they used the installed utility and copied schema/data.","There is no final recursive inventory of the application directory, so incidental artifacts from compilation such as bytecode cache files cannot be conclusively assessed."]}
